From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] A page per controller, honoured by menu and games alike (RelicOS)

Asked for on the device (M22 build 20): the per-pad choices in one place,
and the same choice in the menu and in the games -- build 20's BUTTONS BY
LABEL changed the games and not the menu, which was confusing.

CONTROLLER SETTINGS gets a CONTROLLERS group, one entry per connected
pad (the handheld's own included) opening that pad's page: BUTTONS BY
LABEL (external pads), SWAP A AND B, SWAP X AND Y, PREFERRED PLAYER 1.
All of it lives in relicos.conf under controllers.<guid>.* (the
preferred pad as controllers.player1.guid, so it is one at a time) and
is applied in two places from the same keys: InputConfig::relicosName,
at lookup time, so es_input.cfg keeps the label map it has and the ES
reads it by position or by label per pad, with the swaps on top; and
relicos-pads, for RetroArch.

Player order: the menu's PLAYER ASSIGNMENTS, then the preferred pad,
then the handheld first -- the pad that is always there and can still
leave a game when a connected one goes away -- then the rest by device
node. "No internal controls found!" is no longer logged when the
handheld was simply assigned already.
---
